  ⚠ svelte(prefer-derived-over-derived-by): Unnecessary `$derived.by(...)`. Use `$derived(...)` instead.
   ╭─[prefer_derived_over_derived_by.tsx:2:16]
 1 │ <script>
 2 │     let doubled = $derived.by(() => count * 2);
   ·                   ────────────────────────────
 3 │ </script>
   ╰────
  help: The callback is a single expression, so `$derived(expression)` says the same thing.

  ⚠ svelte(prefer-derived-over-derived-by): Unnecessary `$derived.by(...)`. Use `$derived(...)` instead.
   ╭─[prefer_derived_over_derived_by.tsx:2:16]
 1 │     <script>
 2 │ ╭─▶     let tripled = $derived.by(() => {
 3 │ │           return count * 3;
 4 │ ╰─▶     });
 5 │     </script>
   ╰────
  help: The callback is a single expression, so `$derived(expression)` says the same thing.

  ⚠ svelte(prefer-derived-over-derived-by): Unnecessary `$derived.by(...)`. Use `$derived(...)` instead.
   ╭─[prefer_derived_over_derived_by.tsx:2:10]
 1 │ <script>
 2 │     let x = $derived.by(function () { return count; });
   ·             ──────────────────────────────────────────
 3 │ </script>
   ╰────
  help: The callback is a single expression, so `$derived(expression)` says the same thing.
